On Sunday 07 September 2003 02:48 am, Alex Chupakhin wrote:
> I tried to compile latest 2.6.0 test kernel under 164SX
> RedHat 7.2 binutils 2.13.2.1
> and Gentoo 1.4 binutils 2.13.90.0.18  for  testing
>
> And error occured duringcompilation:
>
> LD .tmp_vmlinux1
> error 139
>
> What is the error

That would probably be a segmentation fault (SIGSEGV).

While I don't personally use Gentoo, I do know that 
binutils-2.13.2.1 and earlier has some problems with very recent 
glibc (say, 2.3.2).  The problem manifests itself as a 
segmentation fault in ld, which is exactly what you're getting 
here.

The problem is fixed in binutils-2.14.  One or two other 
Alpha-related problems are fixed as well.  I'd advise you to 
upgrade binutils and try again...

> and does anybody compiled this kernel successfully?

I personally have not.  I have enough gray hair already, without 
trying beta kernels. ;-)  I've heard pretty good reports on it 
so far though.

-- 
Kelledin
