>and I assume everyone else's was as well.
>
>If this is a case of assiduous filtering, perhaps the list's filter could be
>reset to allow messages that contain some thing like "AXP rules!" in the
>subject line, which we would all include, but which the spoofers would not?
>
>Just a thought, from the decks of a commandeered (Windows) PC

The mailing list only permits subscribers to post.  Any 
non-subscribed posters will get caught in the admin queue and 
rejected, including all spam.

All of the common Windows email viruses right now forge random 
email addresses on the From: line.  If they randomly select 
"axp-list@redhat.com" as the address they're forging, then people 
who receive the virus, will think that it come from axp-list.

Likewise, almost _all_ SPAM generation software does the same 
thing and forges the From: line.

There is absolutely nothing that we (or anyone else) can do about
this other than destroying the entire human race.



