I see it says 750mhz cpu. I had an idea if this is a problem maybe you could
buy a lesser watt psu as 750w psu seem fairly pricey. and then underclock
the cpu if that is possible with a 650w psu as they seem cheaper according
to.....

http://www.pricewatch.com/menus/m297.htm

&

http://www.pricewatch.com/

Just a thought. Maybe it would be a little less speedy. But a stable system
is at least half the battle IMHO even if it's not running at full pelt, and
i wouldn't say no to a dual 650mhz 21264 8mb cache system. Well even if it
didn't dim the house lights in the middle of the night i'm not sure i
wouldn't  ;-)))))))))))))

btw I ran my dual piii xeon 550mhz 1mb cache system at 300mhz for quite a
long while until I was able to buy some nice slimline heatsinks with fans.
And there were no adverse effects.

Anyway hope this helps again.

cheers,


