to build:
1) get & build gnu gcc 3.2.2, gnu binutils.
2) I forgot where I got "ant"
3) The JDK did of course come from Compaq. u will also need the "other" 
 compaq libraries to get java to run. I dont think u need a lic. for the 
jdk or the libraries.
4) get and install from the RH 9.0 SRPMS CD 
:/mnt/cdrom/SRPMS/openoffice-1.0.2-4.src.rpm
5) cd to /usr/src ( the root of /usr/src/redhat/ )
6) tar xjf LX164.OpenOffice.Patches.3.tar.bz2
7) cd /usr/src/redhat/SPECS
8) rpmbuild -bp --nodeps LX2.openoffice-1.0.2.spec
9) cd /usr/src/redhat/BUILD/oo_1.0.2_src
10) cd *office
11) ./configure --with-jdk-home=/usr/java/jdk1.3.1/ 
--with-ant-home=/usr/ant/jakarta-ant-1.5.1
12) cd ..
13) dmake  ( after about 20 hours I get a circular dependency error )
14) dmake ( Apparent it fixes itself )
15) DONE

