As someone already mentioned, it it a hot-swap power supply for a Compaq
Proliant 7000/8000 series server.  It has modular connectors designed to
go into a backplane, so you will not be able to easily use it on your
ATX style PC board.  On the other hand, it is designed to work with a
redundant power supply, so it's possible to daisy chain it with another
one like it, but again, in that Proliant backplane, and under control
of the power management thingy in the chassis.

