I know about that. It screws up one of my spam filters, and
also makes a mockery of missing host error messages for every
tool that uses host names. The "delegation-only" patch would
allow me to work around that knumbskull VeriSign stunt so
that everyone in my domain gets useful error messages for ftp,
ssh, telnet, mail, ....

(They have an http server on that 64.94.110.11 host, but
nothing else. It is said to have an SMTP stub so that mail
accidentally delivered times out instead of failing. Sheesh!)
