On ftp://alpha.crl.dec.com/pub/linux/RedHat/7.2-alpha/updates/ is:

Updated Perl packages that fix a security issue in Safe.pm and a cross-site
scripting (XSS) vulnerability in CGI.pm:
	https://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2003-256.html


The new files are:
	perl-5.6.1-36.1.72.alpha.rpm
	perl-CPAN-1.59_54-36.1.72.alpha.rpm
	perl-NDBM_File-1.75-36.1.72.alpha.rpm
	perl-CGI-2.752-36.1.72.alpha.rpm
	perl-DB_File-1.75-36.1.72.alpha.rpm
	perl-suidperl-5.6.1-36.1.72.alpha.rpm

The perl-suidperl rpm is a new binary that is generated from the perl source 
(src) rpm.  Due to this new rpm, the "rpm -Fvh perl*" will not work, as the 
installation of the other rpms is depends upon perl-suidperl rpm.  

For upgrades, please use:
	rpm -Uvh perl*




Best Regards,



--George



