Hello everybody,

Sorry to bother, but I've found no solution to the following problem: I have a Promise
PDC20268 IDE controller in my XP1000 (ev6) connected to a harddisk(hde) and a CDROM drive (hdg).
DMA is enabled for the harddisk. When I use that harddisk, the machine locks up sooner or later.
dmesg reports DMA initialization problems (see below), and I also get sporadic DMA errors during
disk usage.

This hardware setup worked with the old IDE drivers (kernels prior to 2.4.21), so I don't think I
have a faulty hardware. AFAIK, the PDC202XX_NEW kernel driver should work for x86 PCs. Is this an
alpha specific problem? Is there a fix?

Thanks!
	Oliver


