First off, while I haven't followed the kernel threads, but I believe 
Hendrick's ATA work get yanked around this time?

Secondly, I have seen the _exact_ same problem on x86 with _any_ ATAPI device.  
No issues with ATA, just ATAPI/removables.

It's kinda funny to see it happen with DVD-RAM, because DVD-RAM is the _only_ 
optical drive that does "verify after write" and it catches a crapload of 
errors.  Other optical drives kinda silently "screw up" on me.

I'm running with the latest Red Hat 2.4.20-20.9 kernel on x86 (AMD766 
southbridge), and my ATAPI issues seem drastically reduced.


